shared billing rules
====================

billing_rules.c is the only implementation of the rules that decide what a
customer owes. There is no second copy in another language:

  meridian-telco   billing/invoice.cpp links billing_rules.o directly
  vantage-telco    vendors billing_rules.c and billing_rules.h under
                   vendor/billing-rules/, builds them into a shared object and
                   calls it through ctypes (app/billing/rules.py)
  java/vantage-report
                   cannot call the object, so it is held to the conformance
                   vectors generated here instead

files
-----

  billing_rules.h          the C api, safe to include from C++
  billing_rules.c          the rules
  gen_vectors.c            writes the two vector files below
  conformance_vectors.csv  one row per rule call: rule,arg1,arg2,arg3,expected
  invoice_vectors.csv      whole invoices: account fields, then every line
  AMBIGUITIES.md           the cases nobody has ruled on

Both csv files are generated. `make vectors` rewrites them, `make check` fails
when the checked in copies no longer match what the rules produce.

changing a rule
---------------

  1. edit billing_rules.c here
  2. make check          (rules and vectors)
  3. make register       (the invoice register moves or it does not)
  4. in vantage-telco:   make sync-rules   then   make test parity

Step 4 is not optional: vantage-telco's build fails while its vendored copy
differs from this one by so much as a byte.
